                <pb facs="0468" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg384"/>

                <head>No. 194.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L.
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 18, 1886</date>.
                        [Received June 19.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Sir Lionel West presents his compliments to Mr. Bayard, and has the honor to
                    transmit to him herewith the accompanying acts, which have been forwarded to
                    him, at the request of Sir John McDonald, by the deputy minister of marine and
                    fisheries, for his information.</p>






